Package: mcp-server-ms-365
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 nodejs (>= 18),
 hicolor-icon-theme,
Provides: ms-365-mcp-server
Replaces: ms-365-mcp-server (<< 0.136.1~)
Breaks: ms-365-mcp-server (<< 0.136.1~)
Description: MCP server for Microsoft 365 mail, calendar and to-do tasks
 A Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets LLMs interact with
 Microsoft 365 through the Graph API: mail (Outlook), calendar and
 Microsoft To Do tasks, plus optional presets for files, contacts,
 Excel and Teams.
 .
 Authentication uses MSAL (device-code or app credential flow). This
 package vendors its production npm dependencies under
 /usr/share/ms-365-mcp-server, since the bulk of the upstream Node.js
 dependency tree (Azure SDK, MCP SDK, and friends — some 240 packages)
 is not available in the Debian archive.

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-ms-365
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.6.0),
 mcp-server-ms-365 (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: Registers Microsoft 365 MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for mcp-server-ms-365. Installing it registers the
 ms-365-mcp-server binary as an available MCP server in the local
 mcprack instance; removing it unregisters it again.
